<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis (Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-5> ;
    schema:about "Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D solver of the culminant, tip-growth (non-uniform) stalk elongation, chemotactic cell movement, or that Turing rings on a stalk are an observed Dictyostelium phenotype; a digitized comparison with Martiel & Goldbeter's own time-series figures; spatial (Turing) analysis of the PDE-extended model",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact equilibrium, Jacobian, Hopf curve, d_c(a,b), planar dispersion sigma(k^2) and its Turing band (q_-, q_+); RK4 limit-cycle ODE; 2D pseudo-spectral RD solver with 5 regimes and a 7-point d sweep; SHA-256-locked specimen segmentation (Pass 2)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: First-order and Michaelis–Menten PDE sinks with closed-form equilibria, analytical + numerical Hopf thresholds, Martiel–Goldbeter relay integration and k_e sweep, dimensionless pulse-shape comparison (Pass 3 R2)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Five Lean 4 theorems (Laws 1-5) mirrored by integer checks in --self-test",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Hemispherical-mound RD solver with exact Laplace–Beltrami propagators, spherical-harmonic (Legendre) power spectrum, mound-radius sweep against l*(R) and hexagonal packing, critical mound radius R_min; elongating-stalk solver with ring-count kymograph (Pass 3 R1)",
        "reported_in_source: Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on uniformly growing domains reaction-diffusion patterns undergo frequency-doubling with a dilution term -(L'/L) u",
        "reported_in_source: Gerisch & Hess (1974): suspended D. discoideum cells show spontaneous cAMP-controlled oscillations with a period of several minutes (~5-10 min)",
        "reported_in_source: Martiel & Goldbeter (1987): a 3-variable receptor-desensitization model (rho_T, beta, gamma) with extracellular PDE rate k_e produces autonomous cAMP oscillations and relay",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979): the tri-molecular cubic autocatalytic scheme has a unique positive steady state (a+b, b/(a+b)^2), a Hopf curve b - a = (a+b)^3 and, beyond it, a Poincaré–Bendixson limit cycle",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952): differential diffusion destabilizes a stable reaction equilibrium in a finite wavenumber band; on a sphere the unstable modes are spherical harmonics",
        "transfer_boundary: Mound radius R, stalk radius 0.08 and lengths 1->4 are in the dimensionless planar domain units (L = 6); they are NOT calibrated to the specimen's 32.9 px sorus diameter or stalk length, so the curved-geometry results are predictions of the model's own scaling, not specimen measurements",
        "transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg u is identified with extracellular cAMP for the PDE sink; the 2-species model has no receptor variable, so the pulse-shape comparison with Martiel–Goldbeter is dimensionless (duty cycle, fold change, waveform r = 0.78), not a time-scale match",
        "transfer_boundary: The Martiel–Goldbeter parameter set is the widely used Table I set; with it this implementation gives a 10.68 min period at k_e = 5.4 min^-1, above the ~7 min (5-10 min) Gerisch & Hess anchor; the discrepancy is reported, not tuned away" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Dictyostelium discoideum" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Slime Molds & Bacteria" ;
