<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every new modelling function carries a docstring naming its source: the Laplace–Beltrami ladder and spherical-harmonic eigenvalues (L833-858, Lean Law 4), the critical mound radius formula (L799-806), the Crampin–Gaffney–Maini uniform-growth form (L1007-1030), the first-order PDE scaled trace mirroring Lean `schnakenberg_pde_scaled_trace` (L427-437), the Michaelis–Menten quadratic (L450-461) and the Martiel–Goldbeter f1/f2/Y/Phi definitions with the physical meaning of each parameter commented inline (L158-173, L587-601). Section banners 3b and 4b label the remediation item they close. Deductions: equation numbers of the Martiel–Goldbeter paper and of Crampin et al. are deliberately not cited because they were not re-verified against the PDFs in this pass (-4); the spot-count threshold 0.55 std and the ring threshold (profile mean) are heuristics without a source (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py L944–L964: count_hemisphere_spots threshold mean + 0.55 std and seam merging are uncited heuristics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py#L944-L964>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 core unchanged (exact equilibrium, Jacobian, Hopf curve, d_c, dispersion; L202-340). Pass 3 adds (i) the Laplace–Beltrami operator on the hemisphere discretised as a conservative sin(theta) finite-volume ladder per azimuthal Fourier mode with the no-flux equator and the pole flux vanishing identically, advanced by exact exp(dt D L_m) propagators from the symmetrised eigenproblem (L833-914; constant annihilation < 1e-9 checked at L1859-1861); (ii) the uniform-growth Lagrangian form with dilution (L1007-1076); (iii) the first-order and Michaelis–Menten PDE sinks with closed-form equilibria and Jacobian traces (L427-492) whose generalized Hopf curve is proved in Lean Law 5; (iv) the Martiel–Goldbeter f1/f2/Phi kinetics (L587-609). Deductions: the geometry is a surface reduction, not the 3D culminant, and stalk growth is uniform rather than apical (-3); the Martiel–Goldbeter reproduction gives T = 10.68 min at k_e = 5.4 whereas the model is usually quoted near 7-9 min, so either a parameter or the published figure value is unverified here (-3); the implicit identification of Schnakenberg u with extracellular cAMP is an assumption (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py L1007–L1012: Stalk growth is uniform exponential in a Lagrangian frame; real culmination is apical/tip growth — a reduced model, stated in the docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py#L1007-L1012>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1188-1402) now returns 18 reference-anchored measurements: the 9 Pass 2 metrics plus sub-threshold mound std_u = 0.000 (ref 0), l_dom = 6 vs l* = 6 at R = 1.0 (6/6 radii within +-1), 18 spots vs 18.42 hex-packing at R = 1.5, stalk ring count 3 vs L/lambda_c = 4.25 and ring wavelength 1.333 inside the band (0.576, 1.615), Lean-instance scaled trace 0 (ref 0), numerical Hopf onset 0.12487 vs analytical 0.12486, Martiel–Goldbeter period 10.68 min vs ~7 min, and duty cycle 0.044 (Schnakenberg) vs 0.182 (Martiel–Goldbeter) with waveform r = 0.779. Deductions: most new references are the model's own linear theory (internal consistency) rather than specimen or literature values (-5); the single new literature anchor is missed by 53 % and the anchor itself (7 min) is an approximate reading of Gerisch & Hess rather than a tabulated value (-4); the stalk ring count lags the naive L/lambda_c by 1.25 rings, which is explained (band-edge persistence) but not independently validated (-3); no specimen-derived morphometric is added (0 vs v2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py L176–L176: CAMP_PERIOD_REFERENCE_MIN = 7.0 is an approximate reading (~5-10 min) of Gerisch & Hess 1974, not a digitised figure value; the Martiel–Goldbeter run gives 10.68 min <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py#L176-L176>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-2d-turing-critical-wavenumber-k-star-vs-analytical-k-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-2d-turing-wavelength-lambda-star-vs-analytical-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-dictyostelium-specimen-agar-substrate-2d-fft-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-dictyostelium-specimen-inter-sorus-spacing-to-diameter-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-dictyostelium-specimen-sorocarp-spore-head-diameter-d-sorus>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-differential-vs-equal-diffusion-control-contrast-ratio-d-18-vs-d-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-elongating-stalk-annular-ring-count-at-final-length-l-4-0-vs-l-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-elongating-stalk-final-ring-wavelength-l-n-vs-analytical-lambda-c-must-lie-inside-the-turing-band>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-hemispherical-mound-r-1-0-dominant-spherical-harmonic-degree-l-dom-vs-linear-prediction-l>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-hemispherical-mound-r-1-5-turing-spot-count-vs-hexagonal-packing-prediction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-hemispherical-mound-sub-threshold-radius-r-0-10-r-min-stays-homogeneous-std-u>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-hopf-bifurcation-curve-trace-residual-max-tr-j-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-linear-pde-generalized-hopf-locus-scaled-trace-at-a-b-kappa-1-9-4-lean-law-5-instance>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-martiel-goldbeter-1987-extracellular-camp-oscillation-period-at-k-e-5-4-min-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-michaelis-menten-pde-hopf-threshold-k-e-hopf-0-10-0-90-k-m-1-numerical-onset-vs-analytical>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-pulse-shape-comparison-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-duty-cycle-vs-martiel-goldbeter-relay>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-schnakenberg-autonomous-limit-cycle-oscillation-period-t-lc>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-measurement-schnakenberg-critical-turing-diffusivity-ratio-d-c-0-10-0-90>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-morphometric-validation-3> ;
