<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 89.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py` (overall 89.8/100 vs 90.2 in Pass 2; supersedes audit 2026-10-19-limit-cycle-turing-audit-v2). Both Pass 2 remediation items are closed in the model rather than the presentation: the Schnakenberg PDE now runs on a hemispherical mound and an elongating stalk with the spherical-harmonic ladder, critical mound radius R_min = 0.1297 and hexagonal-packing spot counts verified against the solver (l_dom = l* at 5/6 radii, +-1 at the sixth; 18 vs 18.4 spots at R = 1.5; 0 pattern at R < R_min), and extracellular phosphodiesterase kinetics are modelled three ways (first-order with a Lean-proved generalized Hopf curve, Michaelis–Menten with analytical/numerical Hopf onset agreeing to 0.006 %, and the Martiel–Goldbeter relay with a k_e sweep spanning its oscillatory window 2-7 min^-1). Five Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys), 18 reference-anchored measurements, a 16-check self-test and a byte-identical PNG back the claims. The score does not rise because the new work exposes the next layer: the curved geometries are not calibrated to the specimen, the Martiel–Goldbeter period (10.68 min) misses the literature anchor (~7 min), the stalk ring count (3) lags L/lambda_c (4.25) and only the ODE form of the PDE-extended model is analysed. Overall 89.8/100 (faithfulness 88.8, reproducibility 92.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 3aaa03d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/limit_cycle_turing_comparison.png: rendered output of 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py at 3aaa03d, image/png, 980330 B, 2940×2310 px, artifact_sha256 a323c621aa63149ccc29db5fba8d855d51e45cdd34cffd63205b81f1dff7e9e7 (sha256 a323c621aa63149ccc29db5fba8d855d51e45cdd34cffd63205b81f1dff7e9e7), spec_fingerprint 2171bdf8211cc376e4fec882bcd645f848050c6a4e0c6d15ce22984bb3384713. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2171bdf8211cc376e4fec882bcd645f848050c6a4e0c6d15ce22984bb3384713; artifact_sha256: a323c621aa63149ccc29db5fba8d855d51e45cdd34cffd63205b81f1dff7e9e7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/limit_cycle_turing/dictyostelium_specimen.jpg=e2d2b739211bda97..., datasets/limit_cycle_turing/limit_cycle_turing_reference.json=cc22252b314c8bb8..., datasets/limit_cycle_turing/scout_manifest.json=e71deffb9f317a88...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-limit-cycle-turing-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979): the tri-molecular cubic autocatalytic scheme has a unique positive steady state (a+b, b/(a+b)^2), a Hopf curve b - a = (a+b)^3 and, beyond it, a Poincaré–Bendixson limit cycle | Turing (1952): differential diffusion destabilizes a stable reaction equilibrium in a finite wavenumber band; on a sphere the unstable modes are spherical harmonics | Martiel & Goldbeter (1987): a 3-variable receptor-desensitization model (rho_T, beta, gamma) with extracellular PDE rate k_e produces autonomous cAMP oscillations and relay | Gerisch & Hess (1974): suspended D. discoideum cells show spontaneous cAMP-controlled oscillations with a period of several minutes (~5-10 min) | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on uniformly growing domains reaction-diffusion patterns undergo frequency-doubling with a dilution term -(L'/L) u; reconstructed_in_script: Exact equilibrium, Jacobian, Hopf curve, d_c(a,b), planar dispersion sigma(k^2) and its Turing band (q_-, q_+); RK4 limit-cycle ODE; 2D pseudo-spectral RD solver with 5 regimes and a 7-point d sweep; SHA-256-locked specimen segmentation (Pass 2) | Hemispherical-mound RD solver with exact Laplace–Beltrami propagators, spherical-harmonic (Legendre) power spectrum, mound-radius sweep against l*(R) and hexagonal packing, critical mound radius R_min; elongating-stalk solver with ring-count kymograph (Pass 3 R1) | First-order and Michaelis–Menten PDE sinks with closed-form equilibria, analytical + numerical Hopf thresholds, Martiel–Goldbeter relay integration and k_e sweep, dimensionless pulse-shape comparison (Pass 3 R2) | Five Lean 4 theorems (Laws 1-5) mirrored by integer checks in --self-test; transfer_boundary: Mound radius R, stalk radius 0.08 and lengths 1->4 are in the dimensionless planar domain units (L = 6); they are NOT calibrated to the specimen's 32.9 px sorus diameter or stalk length, so the curved-geometry results are predictions of the model's own scaling, not specimen measurements | The Martiel–Goldbeter parameter set is the widely used Table I set; with it this implementation gives a 10.68 min period at k_e = 5.4 min^-1, above the ~7 min (5-10 min) Gerisch & Hess anchor; the discrepancy is reported, not tuned away | Schnakenberg u is identified with extracellular cAMP for the PDE sink; the 2-species model has no receptor variable, so the pulse-shape comparison with Martiel–Goldbeter is dimensionless (duty cycle, fold change, waveform r = 0.78), not a time-scale match; does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D solver of the culminant, tip-growth (non-uniform) stalk elongation, chemotactic cell movement, or that Turing rings on a stalk are an observed Dictyostelium phenotype; a digitized comparison with Martiel & Goldbeter's own time-series figures; spatial (Turing) analysis of the PDE-extended model." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py:1007-1076 and 1079-1084 — stalk elongation is uniform exponential growth with a profile-mean ring threshold; implement apical (tip) growth with a moving boundary and compare the ring-count ladder with the uniform case, and replace the heuristic ring counter with a Fourier/zero-crossing wavelength estimate so the 3 vs 4.25 discrepancy is quantified as a wavelength, not a count.",
        "remediation needed: 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py:153 and 1007-1016 — MOUND_RADII and the stalk geometry (R_stalk = 0.08, L0 = 1, L1 = 4) are dimensionless model units with no link to the specimen; calibrate R_mound and R_stalk/L from the segmented sorus diameter (32.9 px, L1114-1130) and a measured stalk length so the curved-geometry panels become specimen comparisons rather than model-internal checks, and add a px-per-domain-unit scale to the D1/D3 panels.",
        "remediation needed: 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py:158-176 and 612-638 — the Martiel–Goldbeter run gives T = 10.68 min at k_e = 5.4 min^-1 against the ~7 min anchor; re-read the Table I parameters and the period from the 1987 paper (and Tyson et al. 1989), digitise one published gamma(t) trace, and replace CAMP_PERIOD_REFERENCE_MIN = 7.0 with a tabulated value and uncertainty.",
        "remediation needed: 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py:450-492 — only the homogeneous ODE of the PDE-extended model is analysed; derive d_c(a, b, k_e, K_m) and the Turing band with the Michaelis–Menten sink, run the planar and hemispherical solvers with k_pde > 0, and report how PDE degradation shifts lambda_c and R_min (the spatial consequence the remediation item ultimately asks for).",
        "remediation needed: 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py:917-941 and 967-1004 — the Legendre power spectrum uses the even-reflected cap on a cell-centred grid (only l+m even modes survive) and a 500-step transient; use Gauss–Legendre quadrature on the full reflected sphere, report the power fraction in l*, l*+-1, and run the radius sweep to a converged (>= 1500-step) state so the +-1 tolerance can be tightened.",
        "remediation needed: morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_002_limit_cycle_turing.lean:97-110 — Law 4 proves the finite band only at concrete degrees l = 0..3; add the general statement that det_J(18, l(l+1)) > 0 for all l >= 3 (nonlinear Nat inequality) so the \"finitely many unstable degrees\" claim is machine-checked in general rather than by instance." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.98e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "In addition to the Pass 2 sweeps (5 regimes, 7-point d sweep, CLI overrides), Pass 3 adds three swept parameters whose effect is monotone and visible: mound radius R (predicted l* 0,1,2,3,5,6,10 and measured l_dom 0,1,2,3,5,6,9 across 7 radii; spot count 0->18 tracking 2 pi R^2/((sqrt3/2) lambda_c^2); Panel D2, L1597-1614), the Martiel–Goldbeter PDE rate k_e (period 7.07 -> 14.53 min rising monotonically inside the oscillatory window 2.0-7.0 min^-1 and quenched outside it; D4 inset, L1651-1660) and the Schnakenberg PDE rate k_e (amplitude 0 -> 11.8 rising monotonically past the Hopf point; D5, L1662-1684); `--R-mound`, `--ke-mg`, `--Km-pde` are wired to the panels (L1946-1948, L1967-1969). Deduction: the stalk radius and growth factor are fixed (no sweep), and K_m is a CLI knob without a rendered sweep (-4); the R sweep tolerance (+-1 degree) is the resolution of a 500-step transient, not a converged selection (-5)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic seed 1979 throughout (hemisphere, stalk, planar), headless Agg backend, LSODA with fixed tolerances for the relay; two consecutive default renders produced a byte-identical PNG (SHA-256 a323c621...); `--self-test` runs 16 checks (8 Pass 2 + 8 Pass 3, including hemisphere bitwise determinism, Laplace–Beltrami constant annihilation, Hopf-onset parity < 2 %, Lean integer mirrors and reference-table parity) in ~5 s; default render ~7 s (well under the 3 min budget); all CLI flags documented in argparse (L1936-1978). Deductions: dependency versions are recorded only in this audit, not in a lock file next to the script (-4); when `$HOME/.matplotlib` is not writable matplotlib rebuilds its font cache (environment note, not a result change) (-2); the GIF is not checked for byte identity (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Source and data traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "All seven sources carry DOIs in the module header (L28-52), `paper_citations.bib` (7 entries) and the new `pass3_curved_geometry_pde_reference.json`, whose three new DOIs were resolved through the Crossref API on 2026-10-19 and record that in `resolved_via`. The Pass 2 SHA-256 locks on `scout_manifest.json` and the specimen are unchanged (L93-96, L183-195) and the new reference table is re-derived by self-test check 16 (R_min, band edges, predicted l*, Martiel–Goldbeter Table I, Hopf thresholds for three K_m, oscillatory window; L1908-1924). Deductions: the new JSON is not SHA-256 pinned (it is a derived table, stated in the README) (-3); the Martiel–Goldbeter Table I values are taken from the standard literature set and were not re-read from the paper's PDF in this pass (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
